  "upstream": [
    "CVE-2026-73551"
  ],
  "summary": "### Summary",
  "details": "### Summary\r\nEnvoy URL path normalization does not handle `dot` and `dotdot` segments with parameters correctly. For example URL path `/user/..;foo=bar/admin` is not normalized to `/admin` when path normalization is enabled.\r\n\r\n### Affected Components\r\nURL path normalization and path matching.\r\n\r\n### Details\r\nEnvoy's path normalization does not recognize path parameters per [RFC-3986 section 3.3](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3986#section-3.3) This prevents path canonicalization method from removing `dot` or segments preceding `dotdot` with parameters. \r\n\r\n### Impact\r\nURL path confusion between Envoy and upstream service or bypass of path based RBAC or routing policies.\r\n\r\n### Attack vector(s)\r\nHTTP request with path containing `dot` or `dotdot` segments with parameters.\r\n\r\n### Patches\r\nUsers should upgrade to versions 1.39.1, 1.38.4, 1.37.6, 1.36.10 to fix incorrect handling of `dotdot` segments with parameters.\r\n\r\n### Detection\r\nAccess log entries with requests URL paths containing `/..;` or `/.;` sequences.\r\n",
